The previous version branched on `sz == 1`. This version computes the shift without a branch, using `(sz >> 1) - (sz >> 3)`. For the FIT base-type sizes 1, 2, 4 and 8 this gives 0, 1, 2 and 3, so the result equals the original `values.size() / sz`. The rest is unchanged:
- The string case still returns `stringIndexes.size()`.
- The virtual `IsValid()` and `GetType()` calls are untouched.

I have not measured whether removing this one branch makes decoding noticeably faster.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 FieldBase::GetNumValues(void) const
{
    if (!IsValid())
        return 0;

    const FIT_UINT8 type = GetType();

    if (type == FIT_BASE_TYPE_STRING)
        return (FIT_UINT8)stringIndexes.size();

    const size_t n = values.size();
    const unsigned sz = baseTypeSizes[type & FIT_BASE_TYPE_NUM_MASK];
    // sz is one of 1,2,4,8 -> shift 0,1,2,3
    const unsigned shift = (sz >> 1) - (sz >> 3);
    return (FIT_UINT8)(n >> shift);
}
```